{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3feebd58-35d5-4aef-b924-5b4740af67f7",
    "name": "StudyStreak - AWS Smoke Test",
    "description": "Colección corta para demostrar rápidamente el deployment AWS de StudyStreak.\n\nViene configurada con baseUrl=http://3.238.32.75:8080, usuarioA/exampleA@example.com y usuarioB/exampleB@example.com, usando Password12345!!.\n\nEjecuta los requests en orden. Los IDs y tokens se guardan automáticamente. Si usuarioA o usuarioB ya existen en la base de datos, los requests de registro pueden devolver 409; en ese caso puedes ejecutar directamente los logins si las credenciales coinciden.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://3.238.32.75:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userAUsername",
      "value": "usuarioA",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userAEmail",
      "value": "exampleA@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userBUsername",
      "value": "usuarioB",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userBEmail",
      "value": "exampleB@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Password12345!!",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenA",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshTokenA",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenB",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userAId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userBId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "goalId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dailyRecordId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "trackingId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "validationId",
      "value": "",
